WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:00.680
The Shadow of Geo-Front

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.380
- What's that?
- What now?

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:37.460
Look!

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.950
No! This is terrible!

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.870
A calamity!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.800
Yeah, that hole's a real pain
in the butt.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.090
The experts are coming and going
examining the thing.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.510
That's why we've fallen behind.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:28.020
We'd be better off to just
close off the damn hole.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.520
It's become like the
world's newest natural wonder.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:36.480
"The mysterious caverns
at the heart of Tokyo Geo City."

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:38.860
What do you mean?

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.780
Problems can be
a blessing in disguise.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:47.160
The company may want to
open up the caverns to tourists.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.160
Supervision here.
Yeah?

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.500
What?
Another cavern's opened up?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.290
Yeah, yeah. And?

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.130
Got it.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.010
They've found an even larger
cavern on the lower level.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.720
Great.
We can expect more "experts."

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.980
Old man,
aren't you going for lunch?

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.440
Working too hard can kill ya!

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.790
What's going on?
What happened?!

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.170
An underground city, you say!

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.710
Sounds like something straight
out of an old science fiction movie!

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:38.960
It's called Tokyo Geo-City.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.670
Between 100 and 200 meters
underground.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.760
Composed of
several independent units.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.640
They form a ring 40 kilometers in
diameter in the underground network.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:54.180
It's part of Tokyo's
"Blueprint for the 21st Century."

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:58.270
We're heading for
the main central unit.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:04.190
I definitely smell an adventure!
Treasures, ghosts, time capsules!

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.160
What happened to
your time capsule?

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.780
I forgot what I buried
and where!

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.580
Yup, I'll bet the place is haunted!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.330
Ghosts don't exist.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.720
There it is:
The fire department's Pyro Buster!

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:43.610
"We won't allow you to
invade the holy ground"

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.110
I see.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.820
So the man who stole underground
isn't one of your workers.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:50.160
Right.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.450
It figures.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.250
The fire department usually handles
disaster relief with its own Labors.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:01.210
I wondered why you called us.
It seemed like an odd thing to do.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:05.670
The terrorist smuggled a huge
bomb down to the bottom level.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.590
If that bomb goes off, it's the end
of the Tokyo Geo project.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:13.310
We'll have to start from scratch.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.520
- What's that?
- That?

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.900
During construction,
we came across a huge limestone cave.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:27.490
Surprising that such a wonder
existed right here beneath Tokyo!

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:33.700
So this will be a very
dangerous mission.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.200
This is a live bomb.
One wrong step, and...

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.410
BOOM!!

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.080
Let's try to avoid that, shall we?

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.540
Explosions suck.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.340
What are you scared of, Izumi?

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.800
Don't worry, I'll be with you.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.260
Yeah, I'll... Pardon?

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.350
You mean you're gonna
pilot the Ingram?

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.020
Of course.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.230
Captain...!

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.560
Kanuka trained in anti-terrorist
procedure in New York.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.190
She's also a bomb squad expert.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:11.360
So this time, she'll be acting
in command and on the front lines.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:16.450
Besides, dealing with bombs
calls for a calm composure.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.250
Yeah, that too.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:23.380
Izumi, you will follow Kanuka's
orders and support unit 2.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:24.500
Captain...!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.210
You two might as well set out,
I suppose.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.220
C-Captain!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.230
Here's a little present.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.620
Block 8: Nothing here either.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.630
Block 13 is next.
A quick left, then bear right.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.090
Roger.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.890
Izumi, let's move.
Take the lead.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:57.930
Roger.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:14.490
What's wrong?

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.490
Hear that?
It sounded like a creature howling!

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.700
I'm only going to say this once.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.830
This isn't Jules Verne's creation
or the tomb of Masakado.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:29.710
We won't find the buried treasure
or ancient mysteries you're hoping for.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.600
I found it!

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:46.060
- Stop!
- Why?

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:00.490
It's a trap.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:06.250
Bomb located.
It has a trip wire.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.460
We're about to disarm the device.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.210
Roger.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:12.380
- Pretty bad static.
- They ARE underground.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:15.550
They're doing better than I figured.

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.920
What, don't tell me
you were worried, Shinohara?

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:18.970
Who me? Hardly!

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:23.100
They should be busting the perps!
Isn't that what we're here for?!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.270
- To catch the perps?!
- Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.700
Nothing on radar.
No heat signatures.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.990
Looks like
we're alone down here.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:54.000
Don't push yourself too hard.
If you can't do it, come on back.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.880
Our job's not done until
we apprehend the perpetrator.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:59.930
She sure takes her work seriously.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.760
You said there was a cave
on the lowest level?

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:06.470
Yes, but I haven't had a chance
to look at it yet.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.850
I'm outta here.
Shinohara, take over here.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.110
Yamazaki, mind coming
with me for a bit?

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:15.360
Me?

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.530
Captain, where are you going?

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.110
For a stroll with Hiromi.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:23.320
Later.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.040
Is he really a captain?

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.040
Yeah, in his own way.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:34.080
There's only one possibility.
The criminal must be back here.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.000
What do we do now?

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:36.800
Pursue him, of course.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.970
Shouldn't we come back later?

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:45.680
Who's in charge here,
me or you?

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:50.430
Roger.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:14.290
Rex

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.350
Busted.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:43.320
Shouldn't we go back?

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:47.240
We came all this way down,
so let's look around.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.670
These look like they're
from the Tokugawa era.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.020
Kanuka!

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.350
What's wrong Noa?
Come in!

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.790
Oh, my!

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:39.080
I almost wet myself when I saw you
rise up from my sealed-up well!

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:40.840
You didn't bother
with refreshments.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:44.920
I was afraid you were
the Dragon God, returned.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:46.760
Dragon God?

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:53.140
In ancient times, a cruel dragon
plagued this region.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:57.020
Many samurai went to defeat it,
but none ever returned.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.480
But one day,
a holy man happened by.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:03.480
He used his holy powers to seal
the dragon away inside this well.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.780
Then those bones we saw...

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:08.450
were the samurai who tried
to kill the Dragon God.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.410
- Yes?
- Captain!

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.290
I can't reach Noa and Kanuka!

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.830
- I've lost contact!
- What?

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.670
Noa! Kanuka! Come in!
Either of you!

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.080
What're they doing?!

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:22.750
This is exactly why
I should've gone down there!

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:23.960
Be quiet!

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.340
Sea monster?

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:29.970
Yeah.
My one bomb didn't go off.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:34.060
But I still have one more
ticking away in a different place.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.430
It'll wipe out everything!

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.770
Sea monster, huh?

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:41.190
You must mean the
operations tower in Tokyo Bay.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:41.940
What do you mean?

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:46.360
Tokyo Geo-City has a lot of
earth and sand to get rid of.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:50.410
It's carted off through
an underground tunnel...

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.070
and added to the artificial island
of the Babylon Project.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:58.120
The operations tower hoists
the dirt up from the undersea tunnel.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:02.630
An explosion there would
open the tunnel to the sea.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.550
The entire Geo City project
would be flooded.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.010
They'd have to
start over from scratch.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:08.880
Who told you?

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:11.800
What, you mean I'm right?
It was just a wild guess!

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.970
It's at Jonantoki, 1.2 km. Away.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:15.390
Why you dirty little...!

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.350
What about Izumi and Kanuka?

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:21.980
The tunnel under construction
connects to the lower level.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:22.940
They might be trapped.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.610
Are you okay, Kanuka?

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:31.820
The stabilizer in
my right leg is trashed.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:35.120
It was some kind of animal.
It could attack us again.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:39.910
Here it comes!

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.670
My Ingram can't walk.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:46.130
I'll hold him off.
You get out of here.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:46.750
No way!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.010
Officer Izumi, that's an order!

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:01.560
What are you doing?

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.940
I'm disobeying orders,
that's what!

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.860
Grab onto this;
it'll pull us outta here!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:15.450
Hurry!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:16:59.660
One shot left.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.200
I have six.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.880
You beast! You rotten beast!

00:17:58.470 --> 00:17:59.300
Let's get outta here!

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:25.750
I knew we couldn't stop it.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.040
Checkmate.

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:31.500
C'mon.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:48.520
What is it?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.400
There's another bomb here!

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:51.600
How much time's left?

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.400
Eighteen minutes.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.280
We can't disarm it that quickly.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:00.490
We can't let it explode here.
Take it off.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:02.530
Okay.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:07.250
Take it with you! Hurry!

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:29.270
Kanuka, it's coming!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:30.940
We'll have to
make our stand here!

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:36.020
Noa, I can't forgive you
for disobeying orders.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:40.240
But thanks for saving my life.
I'm grateful.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.530
What do you expect?

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:44.490
We're teammates.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:02.880
Time left?

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:04.840
Thirty-two seconds.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.110
Oh no!

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:09.830
We did it!

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:19.630
Noa, are you okay?
Come in! Respond!

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:26.260
So what did you say in your report?

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:27.890
Nothing.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:33.100
They didn't find a body, and
nobody would believe us anyway.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:35.440
That's true.

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:40.400
Clearly, it was a descendant of the
dragons from the middle ages.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.980
It must have adapted to live in
a subterranean environment.

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:45.860
That's the only
rational explanation.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:49.820
Let's just call it a giant monster.
I've always wanted to see one!

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:54.910
Must you insist on
pursuing juvenile fantasies?

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:58.920
How do you explain a dragon
surviving the middle ages?!

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:01.920
I told you,
it adapted to live underground!

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:05.170
Well what about
his wife and children?

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:06.170
Wife?!

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:08.470
What makes you think it was male?

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:09.680
He had a deep voice!

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:11.890
What are they talking about?

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:14.390
Maybe they saw a dragon.

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:15.600
A dragon?

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:18.690
Hey, Noa, did you see a dragon?

00:22:18.690 --> 00:22:21.150
Nope, it was a giant monster!

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:23.650
No, it was a mutant variation
of the dragon species.

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:26.190
Captain, don't encourage them!

00:22:26.190 --> 00:22:30.030
These people already have
a loose grip on reality!

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:34.660
Did it look like
a mythological beast?

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:37.500
It wasn't a mythological beast,
it was a giant monster!

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:45.340
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:49.050
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:55.310
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:02.730 --> 00:23:04.820
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:07.740
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:12.320
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:16.990
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:19.830
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:24.000
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:30.510
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.760
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:38.310
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:41.520
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:45.610
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:51.780
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:57.830
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:04.460
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:09.380
This story is fiction...

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:09.380
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:16.640
The stupid fight
between Noa and I has...

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:18.180
become serious and
made our relationship worse.

00:24:18.180 --> 00:24:19.270
At the same time...

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:23.310
A mysterious Labor attacks our training
session with an outside defense company.

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:27.820
Moreover, the defense company's Labor,
the Toyo Hatta Auto SRX79 was...

00:24:27.820 --> 00:24:30.400
almost used by Division 1.

00:24:30.400 --> 00:24:32.990
And it seems that some shady things
are happening in Oojima desert.

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:36.950
Next time, "Dark Troubles Rising."
Target, locked on!

